{"created": "2026-10-17T18:10:27.832798+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-17T18:10:28.256431+00:00", "id": 23440389, "conceptrecid": "23440388", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23440389", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23440388", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23440389", "metadata": {"title": "A five-list obstruction on an eleven-vertex tree", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23440389", "publication_date": "2026-10-17", "description": "<p>We exhibit an eleven-vertex tree T with ordinary L(2,1) initial-segment palette size 5 (zero-based span 4) and arbitrary-list parameter 6. An explicit assignment of five-element positive-integer lists is infeasible by a short forcing argument. An ordinary five-palette labeling and the known Delta+3 tree list bound give the exact values. This contradicts the universal equality stated as Conjecture4 in Kohl's 2006 Oberwolfach contribution and Conjecture4.4 in her dissertation. Independently chosen outward pendant-path extensions give infinitely many examples of unbounded diameter.</p><p>The known tree bound and Fiala\u2013\u0160krekovski's 2001 cyclic general-graph five-list obstruction are credited. A bounded source audit leaves historical priority and present openness unestablished; no firstness, minimal-order or new-mechanism claim is made. The deposit includes a three-page research note and a portable TeX-source, exact-verification and priority-audit archive. AI tools were used extensively in research, proof development, literature review, computation, internal adversarial verification and writing. This preprint is unrefereed; no external human peer review or formal proof-assistant certification is claimed.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Kriebel, Alec", "affiliation": "Independent researcher", "orcid": "0009-0001-9320-500X"}], "keywords": ["L(2,1)-labeling", "list labeling", "trees", "counterexample", "Kohl conjecture", "arbitrary lists", "exact verification"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.4171/OWR/2006/07", "relation": "references", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1016/j.tcs.2005.09.032", "relation": "references", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "https://nbn-resolving.org/urn:nbn:de:bsz:105-5454783", "relation": "references", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://kam.mff.cuni.cz/kamserie/clanky/2001/s530.pdf", "relation": "references", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/1211", "relation": "isDerivedFrom", "scheme": "url"}], "version": "1.0", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23440388"}}]}}, "title": "A five-list obstruction on an eleven-vertex tree", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23440389", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23440389", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23440389?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23440389", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23440389", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23440389", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23440389/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23440388", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23440388", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23440388", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23440388", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23440389/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23440389/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23440389/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23440389/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23440389:Tree_Five_List_Note_v1.0.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23440389:Tree_Five_List_Note_v1.0.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/ap